window.TOUR_AUDIO_MAP = {"Hello. What is your role in the support center?":{"file":"audio/6f6363219f36ebb2.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"I lead the support center and oversee the overall operation, team structure, and service performance.":{"file":"audio/2b76b06b6949f78e.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"And how do you manage the department day to day?":{"file":"audio/b43e4de1e38ac143.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Through continuous follow-up, coordination with the team, and close monitoring of workflow and performance.":{"file":"audio/89194d778d9058a0.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Can I take a closer look inside the department?":{"file":"audio/f3555be36213c876.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Certainly. Let me introduce the Customer Support Management Team first, then I will show you how we coordinate issues and development requests.":{"file":"audio/fe74bf5874ed7a8f.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Perfect. Let us continue.":{"file":"audio/a282a549a51bb1d1.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"This is our Assistant Head of Customer Support Center. He works closely with me on operations, systems, automation, and internal development.":{"file":"audio/3c073c0425330ff5.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"And this is our Quality Manager. He leads quality monitoring, performance review, standards, and continuous improvement.":{"file":"audio/50078e99d006acf1.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Together, we review issues and improvement needs, agree ownership, and decide the right next action.":{"file":"audio/44905be5a31d2274.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"When an issue requires another department, we do not send an informal message. We first validate the case and prepare the evidence.":{"file":"audio/173bca636548f46e.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Once the issue is clear, we register it in our internal tracking system. That gives us the details, current status, destination department and follow-up history in one place.":{"file":"audio/baaa5c7d7c81ced0.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Before it leaves Support, management reviews the impact and makes sure the evidence is complete enough for the receiving department to act.":{"file":"audio/6357dce925a399bb.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"Then we create the official ClickUp ticket for the relevant department with the complete problem description and supporting screenshots.":{"file":"audio/87f370e59ad62223.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Whether it goes to Backend, VoIP, Marketing, Commercial or Analysis, we keep following both ClickUp and the internal record until the case is resolved.":{"file":"audio/6244b44d891d06bf.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Development needs can start from customer feedback, an employee suggestion, a Support observation, or a Quality finding.":{"file":"audio/04e991d40fef95f2.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"We validate the need as management and decide who owns the change before anything is sent for implementation.":{"file":"audio/6b894232a7d95027.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"If another department owns the change, we record the converted request internally, raise the official ClickUp development ticket, and keep the follow-up visible from our side.":{"file":"audio/4a7d5530d8d3424c.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"If the need belongs inside Support, management can agree to modify an existing tool, automate a process, or create a new internal system.":{"file":"audio/6bf771f4f432c7ce.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Once we agree on the solution, I handle the internal implementation: design, build, automation, testing and deployment.":{"file":"audio/7460716e78e91b03.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"And the result can come back into the quality cycle, so we can confirm whether the change solved the gap or needs another improvement.":{"file":"audio/367fe20aca6e2061.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"At the beginning of each year, the Customer Support Management Team prepares an action plan and defines the KPIs, targets, and criteria we want to achieve during the year.":{"file":"audio/0f3873a18f3d40ba.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"We review those KPIs quarter by quarter — Q1, Q2, Q3 and Q4 — using clear criteria. When we need better measurement or follow-up, we build or improve systems, scripts, reports, and automation to improve the results.":{"file":"audio/bfc6665b89f62b54.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"We also provide periodic reports to Senior Management, including performance results, operational highlights, and important cases that required coordination with other departments.":{"file":"audio/624a4f7204bc203d.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Their feedback, priorities, and requests are reviewed by the Customer Support Management Team and reflected in our follow-up, action plans, systems, and continuous improvement work.":{"file":"audio/39b1c8496a49646a.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"So the same Customer Support Management Team covers issue escalation, development, annual planning, system improvement, performance measurement, and reporting to Senior Management?":{"file":"audio/8f03a90767780743.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. We keep the work connected from planning to execution, measurement, feedback, and improvement. Now let us continue to the Assistant Head systems.":{"file":"audio/2b230e66ad5cb2ff.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Now that I understand your role, can you show me how you manage the operation from here?":{"file":"audio/c459028b9784cf6e.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Certainly. From here I connect daily operations, performance follow-up, system control and cross-team coordination.":{"file":"audio/cc7a51298e5a0ab0.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"And these are the systems you use to keep that work visible?":{"file":"audio/3d3f9abb812f7e67.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. Let me show you the operational systems behind the center.":{"file":"audio/ea5d66fbafea5982.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"That gives me a clear view of how the center is managed day to day.":{"file":"audio/8862c868f9398eed.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. These systems help us coordinate operations, follow performance, and keep the support center running smoothly.":{"file":"audio/84ba4f01798bccac.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Let’s continue the tour and meet our Quality Manager.":{"file":"audio/7d0220e2774d2f91.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Now I understand the operational side. How does Quality turn performance into improvement?":{"file":"audio/0a7ac8ee46e0538f.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"We monitor service quality, review performance, and make sure our standards are consistently applied.":{"file":"audio/cc2c1f3a387c3dd8.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"And how do you monitor that in practice?":{"file":"audio/3906aeb1bc617aed.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Through our quality systems, controls and review tools. Let me show you our Quality Control Wall.":{"file":"audio/42c5c6835c74ea91.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"I can see how the quality process connects monitoring with improvement.":{"file":"audio/312c04ffee8d6edd.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. We use these insights to identify gaps, coach the team, and continuously improve the customer experience.":{"file":"audio/7d0866b4b06e0720.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"You can continue the tour to the next part of the support center.":{"file":"audio/af3521a159695226.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"Do you all use the same quality systems?":{"file":"audio/f91b4fe75c7442f3.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Yes. We work with the same tools and follow the same quality process.":{"file":"audio/5ac6b02e248f8dbb.mp3","speaker":"quality_team","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"We use reports, dashboards, ratings and review tools to monitor performance and support improvement.":{"file":"audio/ad08ac6fb0c2c29c.mp3","speaker":"quality_team","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"Let us show you the systems we use.":{"file":"audio/9835a8f50f0f4634.mp3","speaker":"quality_team","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"So everyone works from the same quality view.":{"file":"audio/eb714c4027553602.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. We review the same systems, compare findings, and keep the quality process consistent.":{"file":"audio/4ac2d74e65fbc020.mp3","speaker":"quality_team","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"Let’s continue the tour.":{"file":"audio/3ba5e85de04041d1.mp3","speaker":"quality_team","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"Before we meet the supervisors, I want to show you one important part of our structure: team placement here is not random.":{"file":"audio/3365eeba7276ddc2.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"So employees are not simply assigned to whichever team needs people?":{"file":"audio/546ded78daa2cb6d.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. Each operational team has a qualification card. At the beginning, only the required starting card is available, while the remaining cards stay locked.":{"file":"audio/796ff426464a338b.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"And once the employee starts that card, what changes in the system?":{"file":"audio/dcbc86c8288685ca.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"The card moves to In Progress, and the system starts tracking the employee's progress through the required path.":{"file":"audio/44a2ef313707f317.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"What is actually inside the card?":{"file":"audio/e752e3a3daf2c773.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Each card contains a team file divided into sections. The number varies by team: some have two sections, some six, and some ten. The employee completes the required section exams and then the final exam.":{"file":"audio/c328defc5fbd56ac.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"After the final exam, does the employee join the team immediately?":{"file":"audio/c4e61b51db1f11ba.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Not yet. After the final exam, the employee spends about seven to ten days doing real tasks in the area covered by that card. Only after that practical period does the card move to Awaiting Team Leader for evaluation.":{"file":"audio/b8f53de164c235fc.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"So the Team Leader evaluates the employee based on that practical work, not only on completing the card?":{"file":"audio/99a4d0e16ee2e2a0.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. The Team Leader evaluates the employee's performance and results during those seven to ten days. Then it moves to Awaiting Admin, where the same post-card practical work is reviewed against clear criteria before the final qualification decision.":{"file":"audio/074cc8a887df9907.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"So when the card turns green, that means the employee is qualified for that team?":{"file":"audio/193d37e6c2963170.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. The card becomes Passed, the employee is qualified for that team, and the next eligible card becomes available.":{"file":"audio/77d7caaf0806b774.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Can the same employee qualify for more than one team?":{"file":"audio/efe247102aec8e76.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Yes — and over time we expect employees to build qualification across more than one card. We value specialization, but we also need flexibility: if one team faces a workload spike or a drop in coverage, qualified employees from other teams can move in, help reduce the backlog, and keep service levels stable.":{"file":"audio/b2ac1725cdf29f0a.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"That is the logic behind the team structure: qualification first, then assignment. Now let us meet the supervisors and see how the daily operation is managed.":{"file":"audio/c8163dba41a05d46.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"What do you focus on during the day?":{"file":"audio/3f581d437c7aa085.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"We operate three shifts, and each shift has its own Supervisor. During my shift, I stay close to the live operation, the team, and any issue that needs immediate follow-up.":{"file":"audio/a57efd25c393fe38.mp3","speaker":"supervisor","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"So your role is more real-time?":{"file":"audio/79f047230eb291e4.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. I monitor performance, support the team, follow escalations, and keep the daily operation on track.":{"file":"audio/079d5fa5cf44dfa2.mp3","speaker":"supervisor","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"Can you show me how you manage that?":{"file":"audio/90eda2fd957dba87.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Certainly. Let me show you the live operation view.":{"file":"audio/990384ed5b794f03.mp3","speaker":"supervisor","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"So the supervisor stays connected to the operation throughout the day.":{"file":"audio/67dd29475767deed.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. The live view helps me react quickly, support the team, and keep the operation moving.":{"file":"audio/ea40edf8f6809646.mp3","speaker":"supervisor","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"Let’s continue to the Team Leaders area.":{"file":"audio/45ab142d02179890.mp3","speaker":"supervisor","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"Do all Team Leaders work with the same systems?":{"file":"audio/3e13cfe438840e75.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"We share many of the same operational tools, but not every system is used by all five Team Leaders.":{"file":"audio/76591c3a99cfbd13.mp3","speaker":"team_leaders","voice":"en-US-EmmaNeural"},"So some systems can belong to a specific group of Team Leaders?":{"file":"audio/a2801dbd3d78fb2e.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. A system may be shared by all five, used by four, or assigned only to the Team Leaders who need it.":{"file":"audio/4b47d7c50e99ce7b.mp3","speaker":"team_leaders","voice":"en-US-EmmaNeural"},"Can you show me how that is organized?":{"file":"audio/07dfcfd362857072.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Certainly. Welcome to our Team Leaders Command Hub.":{"file":"audio/7fc2d6cbd56f9539.mp3","speaker":"team_leaders","voice":"en-US-EmmaNeural"},"Now I can see how the same operation can have different system access across the five Team Leaders.":{"file":"audio/967f6f8a8516b182.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. We stay aligned on the operation while each Team Leader uses the tools required for her responsibilities.":{"file":"audio/c14ceb708f38584e.mp3","speaker":"team_leaders","voice":"en-US-EmmaNeural"},"Before we continue, there is a new part of the operation I want to introduce to you.":{"file":"audio/4232a2cdc9387516.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"New? What problem were you trying to solve?":{"file":"audio/a583df7ef2421b42.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"As the operation grew, we needed a structured place for cases that require analysis, documentation, ownership, and follow-up beyond normal daily handling.":{"file":"audio/143a669e08520095.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"So this is not another level in the job hierarchy?":{"file":"audio/9929330c08eaec2a.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Correct. It is a dedicated committee for structured review: repeated mistakes, escalated issues, WhatsApp cases, employee suggestions and complaints, and Team Leader file reviews.":{"file":"audio/e6c367cf0e0b20c9.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"We call it OPDC. Let us introduce you to the committee itself.":{"file":"audio/b7ce6dea424f4a8d.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"What exactly does OPDC handle?":{"file":"audio/5078eb0a1cc6ce71.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"We review identified mistakes, WhatsApp customer cases, escalated issues, employee suggestions and complaints, and Team Leader files.":{"file":"audio/635d2348f6b5894e.mp3","speaker":"opdc","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"How do those cases reach you?":{"file":"audio/90ffc305436fad4c.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Depending on the case, it may come through the system, through a Team Leader or Quality, through Management, or directly from an employee as a suggestion or complaint.":{"file":"audio/aba3bc2ea480d7cb.mp3","speaker":"opdc","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"And once a case reaches the committee, what happens next?":{"file":"audio/8f2c13024c811d54.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"We assign it, review the details, communicate with the concerned people when needed, document the findings and actions, and keep the follow-up visible until the case is handled.":{"file":"audio/e639463ddcb83216.mp3","speaker":"opdc","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"Do you also review the Team Leader files?":{"file":"audio/95dfe0fadc1419db.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Yes. We check that the files are complete and updated, record our observations, and later verify that the required modifications and circulated instructions were implemented.":{"file":"audio/ee5d7768973cdff7.mp3","speaker":"opdc","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"How do you manage all of these different cases without losing the follow-up?":{"file":"audio/f80cb345dc03c359.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Through one dedicated OPDC system. The workflows are different, but the case record, ownership, status, findings, and follow-up stay in one place. Let us show you.":{"file":"audio/f4304eb657f19179.mp3","speaker":"opdc","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"What am I looking at first?":{"file":"audio/58a81de309ec9db0.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"This is the committee side of mistake analysis. The Quality Manager analyzes one stream of mistakes, identifies root causes, and looks for solutions. OPDC reviews the remaining mistake cases that require committee analysis, documentation, corrective action, and follow-up.":{"file":"audio/e62e98d35e9e0663.mp3","speaker":"opdc","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"And customer cases from WhatsApp are tracked here as well?":{"file":"audio/5d7f420480fb7fbe.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Yes. The case is registered, assigned, followed up with the customer, and the communication details and final outcome are documented in the system.":{"file":"audio/99f5a67fcd398881.mp3","speaker":"opdc","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"What changes when the issue is an escalation?":{"file":"audio/c6a7d88b2679d136.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"The Committee Chair assigns the issue to the appropriate member or members. We review it with the concerned employee and document the notes, findings, and outcome.":{"file":"audio/8aa0d21c730b5985.mp3","speaker":"opdc","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"And if an employee submits a suggestion or complaint?":{"file":"audio/5ca4ba60acefb365.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"If it is reasonable, relevant, and feasible, it is registered and forwarded to Management. Management can approve it, request clarification, or reject it with the reason documented.":{"file":"audio/10c924702e3358f6.mp3","speaker":"opdc","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"So the Team Leader file review is tracked in this same system too?":{"file":"audio/56a91f3819cc19da.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. We record the review findings and later verify that the required updates, modifications, and circulated instructions were implemented.":{"file":"audio/c8cf5f766a6aaab5.mp3","speaker":"opdc","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"So it is one committee and one system, but with different workflows depending on the case?":{"file":"audio/32d0bbfa117dfa52.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. Different workflows, one controlled record and one follow-up point. The purpose is stronger operations, continuous improvement, and ultimately a better customer experience.":{"file":"audio/a57f45ca4f17f9c4.mp3","speaker":"opdc","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"We also compare the results with previous months so we can identify trends, measure improvement, and highlight any area that needs additional attention or a different approach.":{"file":"audio/d088d18938c749e1.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"So the report is not only for visibility. It is also used to decide what should be improved next?":{"file":"audio/2072dbe4de05866b.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. We review Senior Management’s feedback, directions, and priorities, then translate them into follow-up actions, KPI targets, system improvements, or new initiatives. That keeps planning, execution, measurement, and management feedback connected.":{"file":"audio/14e3eb48bb5644a2.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"With that management cycle in place, let us continue with the Assistant Head of Customer Support Center and the systems used in day-to-day operations.":{"file":"audio/c583c5952679e08a.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Now that you have seen how we plan and measure the operation, let us show you how this management team handles problems, development requests, and coordination with other departments.":{"file":"audio/bb4ab7dd98969517.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Official escalation and development ticketing tool":{"file":"audio/11a1450af44f9111.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Internal system used to record case details, status, routing and follow-up":{"file":"audio/300eaf8ff1af6d4d.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Our internal system brings key support operations together in one place.":{"file":"audio/2667205540e914c1.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Tracks employee mistakes and supports structured follow-up.":{"file":"audio/1f1f1a97e0feeaf0.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Gives Team Leaders one place to manage team work and follow-up.":{"file":"audio/62718dd51d5398d9.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Connects employee performance with levels and bonus results.":{"file":"audio/08f7f0ec997aa51c.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Tracks training progress and qualification cards.":{"file":"audio/1b05911dc7a714a2.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"A Google Apps Script reporting system connected to a centralized data source, used to build, save, analyze, and compare monthly Customer Support reports covering workload, reviews, transferred issues, resolution performance, goals, and achievements.":{"file":"audio/4eecc39bddbcc5db.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"An operational analytics workflow used to continuously monitor service data, identify emerging issues, track top destinations and package performance, analyze complaint patterns, and prepare management reports based on operational trends.":{"file":"audio/ed32ddee254a1ea2.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"A custom desktop EXE application connected to a dedicated database, used to manage employee information and provide a complete view of performance, bonuses, quarterly evaluations, schedules, vacations, overtime, and operational records.":{"file":"audio/23a558287d1efa95.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"A performance-based bonus system that evaluates each employee using ticket activity, attendance, task achievement, team classification, review performance, and assigned level, then calculates the employee’s final monthly bonus.":{"file":"audio/f66a19a5c8e5c546.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"A centralized system used to track bad reviews, assign cases between employees, document customer follow-up, monitor review updates or removals, and analyze case status, employee performance, recurring keywords, and weekly or monthly store results.":{"file":"audio/8bd1d6dd53f342c3.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"A two-part system combining a Google Apps Script stock manager with a desktop EXE checker, used specifically to manage and validate WhatsApp numbers for Social Media services and the USA Offer, while tracking valid, invalid, checked, and recheck records.":{"file":"audio/e1b898c610503d53.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"A Google Apps Script system used to manage employee warnings, document violations and deductions, track warning history and employee risk levels, and send standardized warning emails with supporting attachments.":{"file":"audio/6fa56de69b5727c7.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"A custom EXE application connected to a database, used to track Orange customer cases, refunds, compensation, unsupported-device issues, and follow-up actions.":{"file":"audio/8573b201a8a6bdb0.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"A custom script-based quality analysis system used to identify the most frequent team mistakes, understand their root causes, compare trends over time, and measure whether corrective actions successfully reduce recurring issues.":{"file":"audio/7d10f4486e06bbbc.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"A script-based quality control system used by the Quality Team to register employee mistakes, while the Quality Manager reviews the records and validates that every mistake is clear, accurate, and assigned to the correct classification.":{"file":"audio/49fff97ad8c19875.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"A custom reconciliation script that compares sales figures from Power BI with the internal dashboard, identifies differences, records variance notes, and supports scheduled five-day and monthly data validation.":{"file":"audio/ef9e0e1a9185bc6b.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"An employee-focused quality system that organizes each employee's mistakes, analyzes their mistake patterns, and generates an individual file showing the employee's mistakes by team together with the related quality analysis.":{"file":"audio/ba6029ed06a61bef.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"A quality follow-up system that distributes team mistakes to Team Leaders so they can verify whether the related information is already documented in their operational files and update missing knowledge when needed.":{"file":"audio/fcce3390eef89c87.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"A script-based performance monitoring system used to track employees who remain in the D classification because of high mistake rates or insufficient total points, and to follow how long each employee stays in or exits the classification.":{"file":"audio/acbd1e7fd643d1e5.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"A Google Apps Script evaluation system that measures supervisor performance twice each month, ranks supervisors from highest to lowest based on average points relative to working days, and sends their ranking by email.":{"file":"audio/27cf7efed6c615ce.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"A Power BI analytics dashboard used as a key management reference for reviewing operational sales figures and supporting periodic comparison and reconciliation with the internal dashboard.":{"file":"audio/fce43891f95ad529.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"A custom scheduling script used to validate the weekly workforce schedule by checking employee coverage, assigned tasks, required staffing, and two weekend days for each employee before the schedule is uploaded.":{"file":"audio/1dea7bbefec90fa8.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"A workforce planning system where employees submit weekend, compensatory, or annual leave requests, allowing management to review approvals and confirm whether the final schedule remains properly balanced.":{"file":"audio/9e1b4c42bc6a70e0.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"An operational stock monitoring system used to review country availability, identify new vendor numbers, detect countries that are open but missing from the application, and highlight markets that frequently run low or out of stock.":{"file":"audio/2f2b06360f81f845.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"A quality control system used to record Mistakes identified during next-day reviews of employee tickets, emails, and WhatsApp conversations, including language, process, and other service-quality issues.":{"file":"audio/90012d305daf8513.mp3","speaker":"quality_member_female_01","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"A structured QA testing process used for every new application release to verify calls, messaging, purchasing, core functions, and newly introduced features before the version is fully accepted.":{"file":"audio/6796e3549b3abaa5.mp3","speaker":"quality_member_female_01","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"A daily control-panel monitoring workflow used to review refunds, sales, and key dashboard indicators so the Quality Team can quickly identify unusual drops, changes, or operational issues.":{"file":"audio/9b04bf9698be1b2c.mp3","speaker":"quality_member_female_01","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"A control-panel workflow used to prepare returned UK numbers for resale after account deletion, expired subscriptions, or support replacements by activating, testing, and cleaning the associated accounts.":{"file":"audio/bb96a6e1bc0865d2.mp3","speaker":"quality_member_female_01","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"A daily stock monitoring system used by morning and evening supervisors to verify number availability by country, open newly available countries, close depleted countries in the application, and record every stock status change.":{"file":"audio/8ff9dcc1a90ffeba.mp3","speaker":"supervisor_male_01","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"An AI-assisted verification workflow used for spam-blocked accounts to compare a customer selfie with their identity document, record the match result and service-use explanation, and escalate verified cases to the responsible department for unblock review.":{"file":"audio/a2f8c457688199fb.mp3","speaker":"supervisor_male_01","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"An activity tracking system used to record each employee's daily workload across tickets, emails, reviews, WhatsApp, and other tasks, with weekly reconciliation against Helpdesk totals.":{"file":"audio/3a3b3a5a06d516c4.mp3","speaker":"supervisor_male_01","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"A Team Leader quality view used to review the mistakes recorded for employees in their team during a selected period and follow recurring issues that require coaching or operational correction.":{"file":"audio/b13c82b0fe4193ef.mp3","speaker":"team_leader_social_media","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"A Team Leader performance view that shows each team member's operational workload and total completed work, helping the Team Leader follow productivity and compare performance within the team.":{"file":"audio/17aa6ebd738e7024.mp3","speaker":"team_leader_social_media","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"A structured evaluation system used by Team Leaders every ten days to score employees against defined performance criteria, calculate the final result automatically, and generate the employee's evaluation outcome.":{"file":"audio/ec733ade1c8664cd.mp3","speaker":"team_leader_social_media","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"An internal communication system that allows Team Leaders to send direct notifications to individual employees or their full team for updates, meetings, instructions, and operational announcements.":{"file":"audio/a3a4e159d55caf69.mp3","speaker":"team_leader_social_media","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"A live operational knowledge file for the Bad Review Team, covering how employees identify customers behind negative reviews, investigate Apple Store review cases, resolve customer issues, and follow each case until the review is updated or the case is completed.":{"file":"audio/206c9e6cfc843e14.mp3","speaker":"team_leader_social_media","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"A live operational knowledge file for the Subscriptions Team, covering subscription renewals and upgrades, payment verification, store and Stripe transactions, cancellations, deleted-account cases, and the correct procedures for adding or restoring purchased products.":{"file":"audio/8dd642c8d7b6f282.mp3","speaker":"team_leader_social_media","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"A live operational knowledge file for the Data Team, covering eSIM fundamentals, package activation and troubleshooting, APN, roaming and network checks, provider-specific package rules, deleted packages, usage, compensation, and escalation procedures.":{"file":"audio/847b6c5cc6f6cfdc.mp3","speaker":"team_leader_social_media","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"A live operational knowledge file for the Social Media Team, covering number classification and compatibility, WhatsApp and application activation issues, verification codes, blocked accounts, replacement rules, call troubleshooting, refunds, and ticket documentation standards.":{"file":"audio/6302d3e02d44c3e8.mp3","speaker":"team_leader_social_media","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"A live operational knowledge file for the User & Account Team, covering account and ticket handling, purchase and recharge problems, calling plans, number and account troubleshooting, store issues, and the correct documentation and response process.":{"file":"audio/0901171daf0e3d9b.mp3","speaker":"team_leader_social_media","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"An integrated employee portal that gives each employee a live monthly view of completed tasks, performance level, good reviews, bad-review updates, quality mistakes, and the calculated bonus based on their overall results.":{"file":"audio/9f60c6b01c0aaa11.mp3","speaker":"employee_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"A daily operational data sheet used to record customer WhatsApp follow-up and resolution results, chat and WhatsApp activity totals, Orange package compensation cases, and deleted-package recovery attempts for reporting and follow-up.":{"file":"audio/ab0d0102ff8f9fc3.mp3","speaker":"employee_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"A case-tracking system used to record every customer issue escalated to the VoIP department, including the user number, employee, escalation time, and issue reason, so monthly volumes and recurring problems can be measured.":{"file":"audio/9f79d89e5357110a.mp3","speaker":"employee_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"A customer recovery system used to track bad-review cases, record contact attempts and outcomes, and follow whether the customer updated, removed, improved, or left the review unchanged after support follow-up.":{"file":"audio/262af2358f2528d5.mp3","speaker":"employee_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"A script-based outreach system used to contact customers with open tickets, accelerate issue resolution through WhatsApp, record the problem category and follow-up result, and track whether a Google rating was received.":{"file":"audio/d8858b855238582e.mp3","speaker":"employee_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"A support lookup system that provides tested WhatsApp-ready numbers for Social Media, USA Offer, and UK Mobile replacements, together with an application search tool that shows whether specific apps can be activated using the company's numbers.":{"file":"audio/ca3864fc41da62d7.mp3","speaker":"employee_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"An employee self-service system used to request preferred weekend days, annual leave, compensatory leave, and official-holiday compensation, while availability is controlled by schedule capacity and existing requests.":{"file":"audio/aba212a657caee42.mp3","speaker":"employee_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"A centralized Google Apps Script operations system used by the OPDC Committee to assign and follow up customer numbers, manage WhatsApp contacts and customer problems, track case results, and analyze operational mistakes through Manager and Employee workflows.":{"file":"audio/9d0b17846ca044a1.mp3","speaker":"opdc_chair","voice":"en-US-AriaNeural"},"A timed online multiple-choice assessment used after the first interview to evaluate candidates before they can proceed to the training stage, with the candidate required to remain in the exam tab and achieve the minimum passing score.":{"file":"audio/32c4ea57dbe9668d.mp3","speaker":"trainee_male_01","voice":"en-US-SteffanNeural"},"A structured training-card system that moves trainees through department skills step by step, combining learning, assessment, hands-on practice, Team Leader evaluation, and final approval before each qualification card is awarded.":{"file":"audio/0327160b52fb2046.mp3","speaker":"trainee_male_01","voice":"en-US-SteffanNeural"},"Now that I understand how the teams are structured, what does the work look like for the employees themselves?":{"file":"audio/833804ba3023f1e0.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_03","voice":"en-US-MichelleNeural"},"Once we are qualified for a team, we handle customer cases through the tools and systems assigned to that operation.":{"file":"audio/ce839f3d5b5c9959.mp3","speaker":"employee_male_01","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"So the systems you use can depend on the team you are working with?":{"file":"audio/3bb4e6b9fe31e053.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_03","voice":"en-US-MichelleNeural"},"Exactly. Some tools are shared across the support center, while others are specific to certain teams and responsibilities.":{"file":"audio/1a379a85da147418.mp3","speaker":"employee_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"And can one employee work with more than one team?":{"file":"audio/3f23c1562ccab681.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_03","voice":"en-US-MichelleNeural"},"Yes. If an employee earns more than one qualification card, they can support more than one team and use the relevant systems for each.":{"file":"audio/778cb2e7bb91ef83.mp3","speaker":"employee_male_02","voice":"en-US-RogerNeural"},"Can you show me the systems you work with?":{"file":"audio/3cd1b5ab67ff7613.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_03","voice":"en-US-MichelleNeural"},"Of course. Let us show you how the tools support our daily customer cases.":{"file":"audio/c52165c231dedeee.mp3","speaker":"employee_female_02","voice":"en-US-JennyNeural"},"Do all employees use every system shown here?":{"file":"audio/508727aa15d9fc84.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_03","voice":"en-US-MichelleNeural"},"No. The team label shows whether a system is shared by everyone or used by a specific team.":{"file":"audio/cc4ec7bd7f568e6e.mp3","speaker":"employee_male_01","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"So qualification determines not only the team, but also the operational tools an employee works with?":{"file":"audio/e154b9a441e5a1d4.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_03","voice":"en-US-MichelleNeural"},"Exactly. Team qualification and system access work together so each customer case reaches the right people with the right tools.":{"file":"audio/e00db1db9094e666.mp3","speaker":"employee_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"And what happens when a case needs broader review beyond the normal daily workflow?":{"file":"audio/46ccf8cc12f3bee4.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_03","voice":"en-US-MichelleNeural"},"Those cases can move into our OPDC committee workflow for structured review, ownership and follow-up. Let us show you that next.":{"file":"audio/89cc5a20a3c4286c.mp3","speaker":"employee_male_02","voice":"en-US-RogerNeural"},"The EmployeeSystems sheet is ready. Add the systems and screenshots you want to present here.":{"file":"audio/9f5824a7a8bb0249.mp3","speaker":"employee_male_01","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"So the training journey starts with the interview?":{"file":"audio/f046f8913a2868b7.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Actually, it starts even earlier. The Quality Manager and I first review the applications and shortlist the candidates we believe are worth meeting.":{"file":"audio/812eed08673064e4.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"We look at the overall profile, communication background, experience, and whether the candidate appears suitable for a customer support environment.":{"file":"audio/2921802e5c6d76fc.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"And what do you evaluate in the first interview?":{"file":"audio/3cd97539f3624828.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"We keep it conversational. We ask the candidate to introduce themselves and talk about their general experience.":{"file":"audio/2ed8f5c4bfdb6969.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"We also ask simple questions about computer use, Microsoft tools, and basic working habits.":{"file":"audio/3c0ac60398b19a1d.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Do you test English as well?":{"file":"audio/ca185e7a47111515.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Yes. We ask the candidate to read a short English passage so we can understand their basic reading and communication level.":{"file":"audio/c491a389a633556e.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"If the first interview goes well, we ask the candidate to download the Numero app, explore it, and browse the website before the online exam.":{"file":"audio/37a23263249616f9.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"So they are expected to prepare on their own before the exam?":{"file":"audio/35e26500b3caa9dc.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. The exam is general. We want to see whether the candidate took the initiative to understand the product before the next step.":{"file":"audio/a2a799ab7c8f552a.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Is this already a detailed technical support exam?":{"file":"audio/ac02b5f7636d5e65.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"No. It is a general multiple-choice exam focused on basic understanding of Numero, the application, the website, and general product knowledge.":{"file":"audio/91635fedff39ffb3.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"And if the candidate fails?":{"file":"audio/073f3b11d40c5d88.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Then the process stops at this stage. Only candidates who pass continue to the second interview.":{"file":"audio/de4291373111e7af.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"What happens after passing the exam?":{"file":"audio/1520c847338a97ef.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"The candidate returns for a second interview with the Customer Support Management Team.":{"file":"audio/b18ec09748c7dbd5.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"At this point we already have the first interview, the exam result, and a better understanding of the candidate.":{"file":"audio/63d3cefa1080af91.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"We use the second interview to complete the evaluation and compare the strongest candidates.":{"file":"audio/1a8597b30cd05792.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"Thank you. We will review the results and contact you.":{"file":"audio/72c1ac6985436ee8.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"So passing the exam and reaching the second interview still does not guarantee selection?":{"file":"audio/ad3d5ef5ab82f606.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Correct. We may interview several qualified candidates while only having a limited number of positions available.":{"file":"audio/56a977e8fdfe96dd.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Only the candidates selected after the complete review move into the qualification stage.":{"file":"audio/529e2ae4fa7d435c.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Once someone is selected, do they immediately start handling customers?":{"file":"audio/b0a598c239e404d8.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"No. Before independent work, they enter our qualification card system.":{"file":"audio/dbe623866bba1d47.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"They begin with the general rules and best support practices, then move into the first operational card: User & Account.":{"file":"audio/b00efa6011e0f504.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Do you expect high scores immediately?":{"file":"audio/30a8c74d2f410dce.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Not necessarily. This is new material. At the beginning we want them to read, try, learn, and show us how they develop.":{"file":"audio/ba539a305adbedf3.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Each card contains a different number of sections. The trainee progresses through the material, completes the section exams, and eventually reaches the final exam.":{"file":"audio/8cad28b4be2c9043.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"When does the trainee begin working with real customer cases?":{"file":"audio/4cc6097e023a8bb9.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Once the basic knowledge is in place, the trainee joins the shift under controlled supervision.":{"file":"audio/34e226c22bfc44bc.mp3","speaker":"supervisor_male_01","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"The trainee receives a ticket, explains the customer issue, prepares the internal note and the customer reply, then sends everything to the training group for approval.":{"file":"audio/702cab04be8b7cc8.mp3","speaker":"supervisor_female_01","voice":"en-US-JennyNeural"},"And if something in the response is wrong?":{"file":"audio/d96bc108adcb06d9.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"We correct it before it reaches the customer and explain exactly what needs to change.":{"file":"audio/2629871251f23302.mp3","speaker":"supervisor_male_02","voice":"en-US-RogerNeural"},"Depending on the shift and the case, that coaching may come from a Supervisor, Team Leader, Quality Manager, or management.":{"file":"audio/17b1f2b74ae6cc13.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Do you keep approving every reply for the full three months?":{"file":"audio/e76b5922e53e4b48.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"No. As the trainee becomes more reliable, we gradually reduce the approval requirement and monitor the work instead.":{"file":"audio/99782d55791e13f0.mp3","speaker":"supervisor_female_02","voice":"en-US-MichelleNeural"},"If mistakes remain low, the trainee continues progressing. If performance becomes unstable, we step back and reinforce the weak areas.":{"file":"audio/d0b91fc87537cfb4.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"How far do you expect a trainee to progress during the contract?":{"file":"audio/320d46248c3f1edf.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"The goal is for the trainee to become solid in the first operational area during the three-month period. Some progress fast enough to begin the next card as well.":{"file":"audio/26f673222f1d5423.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"What happens when the three months are completed?":{"file":"audio/0ffeac78eb7cc6a7.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"We review the complete journey — performance, quality, progress, behavior, and operational readiness.":{"file":"audio/c0df13ff8c9cd7ca.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"The contract may end, be extended for another month, or move into a one-year contract and continued employment.":{"file":"audio/36cb270d745e02b6.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"So the qualification card system is mainly a trainee program?":{"file":"audio/799226c889674275.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"No. It applies to the entire support center. Existing employees also go through the cards, exams, Team Leader evaluation, and Admin evaluation.":{"file":"audio/462e270d2f30d8c1.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"What if an experienced employee was previously qualified, but their performance later drops?":{"file":"audio/5e54e27a45e05c8d.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Previous qualification does not mean we ignore current performance.":{"file":"audio/d9c6df8a8dc52d02.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"If necessary, we can reset the employee’s cards, remove advanced team qualification, and send them back through the learning path from the beginning.":{"file":"audio/87da2da9746884a3.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Even if they previously worked in advanced teams?":{"file":"audio/b5a1b61fd79c8ad7.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_01","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Yes. The qualification has to reflect the employee’s current ability, not what they were able to do months ago.":{"file":"audio/70d1bfe514e82e31.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"The objective is not to punish people. It is to identify weaknesses early and rebuild the knowledge correctly.":{"file":"audio/71dbcf62cb2155ef.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"Because whether someone is new or experienced, the customer should always be handled by someone who is currently ready for that responsibility.":{"file":"audio/52db297aa0c9b33e.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Before we go through the full recruitment and training journey, let me show you the systems that control the trainee qualification process.":{"file":"audio/7039503f09684c77.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Before we enter, I want to introduce a new area we are currently building: our AI Development and Operational Improvement department. It is still under construction, but the direction is clear.":{"file":"audio/3ba79126eebb49ce.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"The goal is to keep developing the department and stay current with any advancement that can genuinely support the work, reduce time and effort, and improve operational efficiency. Let us go inside and see what we are developing.":{"file":"audio/81582b91374e6638.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"This looks like a new area. Is AI already fully integrated into the support center?":{"file":"audio/634aecd3161a5d87.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_02","voice":"en-US-JennyNeural"},"Not yet. This is a new development area that we are currently building and organizing.":{"file":"audio/e182efa19cf723c2.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"My goal is to review how we work across the support center and identify every place where AI or automation can make the job easier, faster, or more accurate.":{"file":"audio/c3eb7ac966e5b6cb.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"So you want AI inside every process?":{"file":"audio/9ed3d6dc8ff6d32b.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_02","voice":"en-US-JennyNeural"},"Where it actually adds value. I do not want to use AI just because it is available.":{"file":"audio/ca8471a7de2a41b8.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"I want to use it where it can reduce repetitive work, improve analysis, reduce avoidable mistakes, or help us reach better results.":{"file":"audio/24b4f6a5e2edaa30.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"And who is responsible for this initiative?":{"file":"audio/645f0fa98fde0db1.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_02","voice":"en-US-JennyNeural"},"The strategic direction and major decisions are agreed jointly by the Customer Support Management Team. I coordinate the initiative day to day, translate those decisions into operational requirements, and assess which solutions are genuinely useful for the operation.":{"file":"audio/1f87381fa118f3b3.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"I support the research, testing, implementation, and follow-up. We turn approved ideas into small working solutions and test them in real operations.":{"file":"audio/1cfdc0209987b127.mp3","speaker":"ai_employee","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"Have you already built anything that gives you a foundation for this?":{"file":"audio/572903b1a228bbc8.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_02","voice":"en-US-JennyNeural"},"Yes. We already rely heavily on automation and operational tools built with Google Scripts, reports, trackers, dashboards, alarms, verification utilities, number management, scheduling support, and reconciliation.":{"file":"audio/cbb5f519dbfbb600.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Those tools are not all AI, but they give us an important foundation: we already know how to identify repetitive work and turn it into a system.":{"file":"audio/36527ddbfd285ef3.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"That existing automation also gives us real workflows to study, test, and improve instead of starting from zero.":{"file":"audio/87f92f133e3d75be.mp3","speaker":"ai_employee","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"And where have you already used AI itself?":{"file":"audio/37b9b69a216b3168.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_02","voice":"en-US-JennyNeural"},"We have already used AI in specific cases, including matching selfie photos with ID cards and analyzing results in some reports.":{"file":"audio/c488edbb48d05438.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Those early cases help us learn what works well, where human review is still needed, and what can be expanded safely.":{"file":"audio/f918718c1a425f82.mp3","speaker":"ai_employee","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"What do you want AI to do inside the systems employees already use?":{"file":"audio/d0cfb50f6855d3ce.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_02","voice":"en-US-JennyNeural"},"I want the systems themselves to assist the employee while they work — collect information, detect context, organize results, support translation, alert to language or response issues, and guide handling steps where appropriate.":{"file":"audio/47c6b23214be14f4.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Examples we are exploring include eSIM device detection, automatic ticket-note information, sales data aggregation, smarter filtering, ticket sorting, handling guidance, and WhatsApp API integration.":{"file":"audio/b7036afd0c7a0a84.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Our job is to test which ideas can be implemented reliably and which ones actually save time in real use.":{"file":"audio/bf5ae2019b54ce50.mp3","speaker":"ai_employee","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"And outside the ticket workflow?":{"file":"audio/a5ee67e924ce9d1e.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_02","voice":"en-US-JennyNeural"},"That may be one of the highest-value areas. I want AI to help us analyze larger operational datasets and surface patterns faster.":{"file":"audio/7059a7c0df2e2b06.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"That includes weekly schedule creation, stock analysis, package consumption and sales, ticket volume and recurring issues, employee performance, and number replacement reasons.":{"file":"audio/161b990ae918fdd2.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"For these use cases, we can compare AI-assisted results with the current manual process and see whether the improvement is real.":{"file":"audio/5ecb7e0332a09c65.mp3","speaker":"ai_employee","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"With all these possibilities, how do you decide what to build first?":{"file":"audio/f1823c6109ce54c6.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_02","voice":"en-US-JennyNeural"},"We start with the operational problem, not with the technology.":{"file":"audio/d1c24e3dffab6c6e.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"If a task is repeated, takes too much manual effort, creates avoidable mistakes, or produces enough data to analyze, we evaluate whether AI or automation can improve it.":{"file":"audio/3c2fe4718ef2ccf5.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Then we prototype, test with real work, measure the result, and improve it. If it is not useful or reliable, we do not force it into the operation.":{"file":"audio/a3fc96a4dddc099e.mp3","speaker":"ai_employee","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"So the goal is not simply to say that the support center uses AI?":{"file":"audio/c10971bd06617ad7.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_02","voice":"en-US-JennyNeural"},"Exactly. AI is not the objective. Better work is the objective.":{"file":"audio/1d7518790d96bdbe.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"The employee stays responsible for the customer. AI should remove unnecessary effort, give better information, and help people make faster and better decisions.":{"file":"audio/866d0aca2d61cbc8.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"That also means every tool has to be understandable, testable, and easy for the team to use in the real workflow.":{"file":"audio/dc02d40bad30fcf8.mp3","speaker":"ai_employee","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"Where do you want this initiative to reach?":{"file":"audio/d4f789ea5ec37548.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_02","voice":"en-US-JennyNeural"},"I want AI to become a practical layer across the support center — wherever it can help in systems, reports, quality, training, employee support, management analysis, or operational decisions.":{"file":"audio/d4adcb0951647d8d.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Every successful improvement can then become part of the normal way we work.":{"file":"audio/bdb6ecacc64d9a97.mp3","speaker":"ai_employee","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"So this is still the beginning?":{"file":"audio/635c46c1a4a5d3c5.mp3","speaker":"visitor_female_02","voice":"en-US-JennyNeural"},"Yes. We are still building it, but the direction is clear: wherever AI can save time, reduce unnecessary effort, improve accuracy, or help us make better decisions, we want to explore it.":{"file":"audio/0431cdb7280f164f.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Because in the end, systems, training, quality, automation, and AI all serve the same final objective.":{"file":"audio/9dd6a45154acb843.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"After everything I have seen, what is the one thing all of this is ultimately trying to achieve?":{"file":"audio/d8af9e752b04acbc.mp3","speaker":"visitor_male_01","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"Customer satisfaction. Every system, every process, every review, and every improvement exists because there is a person on the other side who needs help.":{"file":"audio/de57026d05c2e6a5.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Sometimes the solution is technical. Sometimes it is follow-up, escalation, explanation, or simply staying with the customer until the situation becomes clear.":{"file":"audio/9af13182829e1015.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"So support is not only about closing a ticket?":{"file":"audio/cb98d7ccc119d789.mp3","speaker":"visitor_male_01","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"Exactly. Closing a ticket is not enough if the customer still feels unheard or uncertain.":{"file":"audio/a040e382c6af4fc7.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"We train our people to listen, explain, solve, follow up, and support the customer as a person — not just as a case number.":{"file":"audio/eef1a5aad503c518.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"And when customers leave satisfied, that becomes the real measure of the operation?":{"file":"audio/b37409300591a953.mp3","speaker":"visitor_male_01","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"Yes. Satisfaction is where all the work connects — management, quality, supervisors, team leaders, OPDC, employees, training, systems, automation, and AI.":{"file":"audio/9ce53d46e3e9d2a8.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"We measure performance because we want to know whether the work is actually getting better — faster handling, stronger quality, fewer avoidable mistakes, and happier customers.":{"file":"audio/a6a3c2a4ea4388f1.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"So the numbers matter because they tell you whether the customer experience is improving?":{"file":"audio/f07d60f6d1749cd3.mp3","speaker":"visitor_male_01","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"Exactly. The number is not the goal. The experience behind the number is the goal.":{"file":"audio/4f2ba41615c9c6a0.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"We will use every system we build, every lesson we learn, every tool we improve, and every new technology we can responsibly adopt to do everything possible for a better customer experience.":{"file":"audio/bfcf7955b6820e6b.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"At the end of the day, the strongest measure of our work is the experience our customers share.":{"file":"audio/cb87b66fdb357034.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Thank you. This visit gave us a clear picture of how the Customer Support Center is managed, measured, and continuously improved.":{"file":"audio/63c175f1b8c2b359.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"We appreciate your visit. Our goal is to keep support structured, accountable, and connected to the wider organization through clear follow-up and measurable results.":{"file":"audio/7381064fd0cfe0f7.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"From plans and systems to reports and coordination, we try to turn daily support work into stable operations and practical improvement.":{"file":"audio/04aacd3d17cac8e9.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"And from the quality side, we keep reviewing performance, identifying gaps, and supporting the teams so the customer experience keeps getting better.":{"file":"audio/569fd863c6469c82.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"Honestly, the structure is clear, the roles are well connected, and the effort of the full team is very visible. It leaves a strong and professional impression.":{"file":"audio/ed1e72f407444f56.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"That means a lot to us. Please share any note or suggestion. We always welcome feedback that helps us improve further.":{"file":"audio/63e277b651e9f3a6.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Thank you again. We are leaving with a very positive impression of the Customer Support Center, its leadership, and the teams behind it.":{"file":"audio/8d05839b6574eb3e.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"You are always welcome. It was a pleasure to host you, and we hope the visit reflected the spirit of this department and the people behind it.":{"file":"audio/78ede1a0a38e78a0.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Certainly. Let me introduce the Customer Support Management Team first, then I will show you how decisions move into action.":{"file":"audio/fd38ed063c553aef.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Every month, we prepare a comprehensive Customer Support report for Higher Management. It gives a clear view of the department’s workload, performance, and the most important operational results from that month.":{"file":"audio/c5f2ab0c8b184a2d.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"The report covers key indicators such as ticket volumes, incoming workload, service performance, recurring issues, and the cases that were escalated to teams such as Backend or VoIP for further action.":{"file":"audio/c63b722d511f2213.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"Exactly. We review Higher Management’s feedback, directions, and priorities, then translate them into follow-up actions, KPI targets, system improvements, or new initiatives. That keeps planning, execution, measurement, and management feedback connected.":{"file":"audio/87b70e3909dea9ef.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Before we meet the Supervisors, let me explain how daily supervision is organized.":{"file":"audio/ee28abf3d99620a6.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"We operate three shifts, and each shift has its own Supervisor responsible for the live floor and coordination during that shift.":{"file":"audio/4e0d1c0c6d4ef36b.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"So the Supervisor is responsible for the whole shift, not only one team?":{"file":"audio/8134583c6e241ebe.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Exactly. The Supervisor keeps the full shift aligned, while Team Leaders focus on their assigned teams, daily coverage, employee support, and team-level follow-up.":{"file":"audio/cd265dc3657d4c4d.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"And how do you decide which employees are placed in each team?":{"file":"audio/eca1f21c701f7ba2.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"Because we support many products, we divide the operation into specialized teams. We prefer specialization, but we also build cross-qualification so employees are not limited to one card and can support another team when workload shifts or extra coverage is needed.":{"file":"audio/88248daded1aa60f.mp3","speaker":"quality_manager","voice":"en-US-EricNeural"},"And where does the committee fit into this structure?":{"file":"audio/2f35a048bdce25c4.mp3","speaker":"visitor","voice":"en-US-AvaNeural"},"OPDC works alongside the operation as a dedicated committee for cases that need structured review, documentation, ownership, and follow-up beyond normal shift handling. We will visit the committee later in the tour.":{"file":"audio/9fb2fbfa7bab415d.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Now let me show you the qualification path that controls team assignment before we move to the Supervisor.":{"file":"audio/9fae2e97c77bae6b.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"Before we meet the supervisors, I want to explain one important part of our structure. We support many products and service areas, so we divide the operation into specialized teams rather than treating every task as one pool.":{"file":"audio/ea1a2501fa0c7c51.mp3","speaker":"support_manager","voice":"en-US-GuyNeural"},"Yes — and over time we expect each employee to build qualification across all relevant cards, not only the card of the primary team. We value specialization, but we also need flexibility: if one area faces a sudden workload spike or a drop in coverage, qualified employees from other teams can move in, support that queue, reduce the backlog, and keep service levels stable.":{"file":"audio/c23b69cd84b07755.mp3","speaker":"assistant_head","voice":"en-US-ChristopherNeural"},"This is the committee side of mistake analysis. The Quality Manager owns the Quality stream: analyzing assigned mistakes, identifying root causes, patterns, and corrective solutions. OPDC then handles the remaining mistake cases that require committee analysis, documentation, corrective action, and follow-up.":{"file":"audio/7aaae57247b4314f.mp3","speaker":"opdc_member_male_01","voice":"en-US-BrianNeural"},"If it is reasonable, relevant, and feasible, it is registered and forwarded to the Customer Support Management Team. The team can approve it, request clarification, or reject it with the reason documented.":{"file":"audio/01f6577233c74246.mp3","speaker":"opdc_vice_chair","voice":"en-US-EmmaNeural"}};
